---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/sections/PageHero.astro';
import { site, addressOneLine } from '../lib/site';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }];
const updated = 'July 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Gupta Enterprises handles the information you send through this website, including RFQ submissions and uploaded drawings."
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <PageHero
    kicker="Legal"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lead="What we collect through this website, why, and what we do with it. Written plainly rather than defensively."
    breadcrumbs={crumbs}
    align="wide"
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="mono note">Last updated: {updated}</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This website is operated by {site.legalName}, {addressOneLine()}. For any question about
          this policy or about information you have sent us, contact
          <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect information in exactly two situations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>When you submit a form.</strong> The Request for Quotation and Contact forms
            collect the details you type into them — your name, company, email, phone, country, and
            the description of your requirement — together with any drawing files you attach.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>When you email or call us.</strong> Ordinary business correspondence, kept for as
            long as the commercial relationship or enquiry reasonably requires.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We do not run advertising trackers or third-party analytics on this site. There is no
          cookie consent banner because we do not set marketing or analytics cookies.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <p>
          Solely to respond to your enquiry: to assess manufacturability, prepare a quotation,
          manufacture and supply parts, and maintain the resulting commercial relationship. We do not
          sell your information, and we do not add you to a marketing list without asking.
        </p>

        <h2>Your drawings and technical information</h2>
        <p>
          Drawings, specifications and technical files you send are used only to quote and
          manufacture your part. They are shared internally only with the people who need them —
          typically our estimating, tool room and production staff — and are not shown to other
          customers or used as reference work without your written permission.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where a finishing operation is subcontracted to a qualified partner, the minimum
          information required to perform that operation is shared with them. Nothing beyond that.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are happy to sign your non-disclosure agreement before you send anything. Tick the NDA
          box on the <a href="/rfq">RFQ form</a> or send it with your enquiry.
        </p>

        <h2>Who processes data on our behalf</h2>
        <p>
          This site is a static website hosted by Netlify, which also receives and stores form
          submissions on our behalf and forwards them to us by email. Netlify processes this data as
          our service provider. Email correspondence is handled through our own business email
          provider.
        </p>
        <p>
          These providers may store data on servers outside India. We use them because they are
          established services with their own security and data-protection commitments; we do not
          transfer your information to anyone else.
        </p>

        <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Enquiries that do not lead to business are kept while they remain commercially relevant and
          then deleted. Records relating to orders we have fulfilled are kept for as long as
          applicable Indian tax, statutory and quality-record requirements demand.
        </p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served over HTTPS and form submissions are encrypted in transit. No system is
          perfectly secure, so if a drawing is genuinely commercially sensitive, tell us and we will
          agree a handling arrangement — including an NDA — before you send it.
        </p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
          delete it. Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> and we
          will respond. Where we are legally required to retain a record — a tax invoice, for
          example — we will tell you that rather than quietly ignore the request.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we change how we handle information, we will update this page and the date at the top.
          Material changes affecting existing customers will be communicated directly.
        </p>

        <hr class="hairline" style="margin: 2.5rem 0" />

        <p class="disclaimer">
          This policy describes our actual practice in plain language. It is not a substitute for
          legal advice, and it does not attempt to recite every provision of the Digital Personal
          Data Protection Act 2023 or any other applicable law. If you require a specific contractual
          data-protection commitment for your procurement process,
          <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we will work to your form of words.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .note {
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }

  .disclaimer {
    font-size: var(--fs-sm);
    color: var(--text-subtle);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
